window.FIGS=[{"id":"fig-audit-modes","src":"book/figures/fig-audit-modes.tex","caption":"Same write, five different things an attacker must beat. The log and the sign-in sheet sit beside the write, so Heron can skip them; the marks in the chapter colour sit on it. The rows are not a staircase: Brokered and Confined defeat different adversaries rather than the same adversary harder. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":1221},{"id":"fig-swk-atomicity-fix","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-atomicity-fix.tex","caption":"Separate commits can leave orphaned writes. One immediate-mode transaction makes the three local writes atomic; no distributed compensation protocol is needed. [internal, OP-11]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":148,"page":64},{"id":"fig-swk-capability-permission","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-capability-permission.tex","caption":"Capability and permission are independent. The shaded case is possible but forbidden, a state that one merged capability-and-permission field could not express. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":113,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-claim-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-claim-lifecycle.tex","caption":"The guarded claim lifecycle as a finite-state machine. Acquire is a single atomic insert against a SQLite uniqueness constraint; re-claim of a held claim and release are idempotent, while a claim on an expired row, even by its holder, is a new acquire; expiry moves a claim to expired , from which a sweep returns it to free : the next read or acquire that checks expiry, or the daemon's periodic cleanup. There is no queued state: losing callers receive 409 Conflict and must manage their own backoff. [internal, alg:acquire]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":98,"page":31},{"id":"fig-swk-commitment-oracle","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-commitment-oracle.tex","caption":"Closure requires a supported evidence reference rechecked by the daemon. Free-text assertions leave the commitment open; scope policy, not the agent, supplies its deadline. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":130,"page":52},{"id":"fig-swk-consistency-model","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-consistency-model.tex","caption":"Overlapping requests receive one commit order: A claims, B loses, A releases, C claims. Theorem states the six assumptions this ordering requires. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":145,"page":63},{"id":"fig-swk-continuity-organs","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-continuity-organs.tex","caption":"The continuity chain as an evidence-support profile, computed from the chapter's own status grades. Checkpoint inherits notes only. The outcome ledger inherits part of that, and identity and market inherit that part with no grade of their own. Downstream confidence cannot exceed the weakest upstream link. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":133,"page":55},{"id":"fig-swk-controllability-quadrant","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-controllability-quadrant.tex","caption":"Exact realization needs control and observations sufficient to evaluate the specified guard. The partial-observation theorem states the full condition. A stricter policy, such as refusing every egress, may preserve safety while rejecting legal histories. Detection outside the shaded cell is not automatic. [internal; schematic]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":126,"page":49},{"id":"fig-swk-delegation-chains","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-delegation-chains.tex","caption":"The designed coordination lineage must be carried inside each signed authorization hop. Authenticating its bytes does not establish semantic task equivalence.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":110,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-durability-dramatization","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-durability-dramatization.tex","caption":"With OS and database/WAL state intact, restart recovers a process-crash commit; power loss can erase an unsynchronized commit. The five-millisecond interval is illustrative.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":92,"page":29},{"id":"fig-swk-enforcement-layers","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-enforcement-layers.tex","caption":"Refusal is not compulsory mediation. Grades are source-reported, not an independent runtime audit.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":152,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-fencing-epoch","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-fencing-epoch.tex","caption":"The epoch, not the lock, is the guard: the broker accepts the epoch-105 write and rejects the stale epoch-104 write. Theorem has the broker read the newest epoch and its holder from the kernel's record, not from the writes it happens to see. Designed, not built (I2b): no broker checks an epoch yet. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":100,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-i12-dependency","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-i12-dependency.tex","caption":"I7--I9 depend on authenticated identity at every write path. A legacy path that accepts self-asserted identity can bypass otherwise correct owner checks; I12 remains partial. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":153,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-idempotency-gap","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-idempotency-gap.tex","caption":"A missing receipt does not reveal whether the effect happened. Twelve local SQLite cases, run apart from the kernel. Receiver deduplication here atomically retains the key, payload, effect and receipt; a sender-side key alone does not supply that contract. [Local fixture, receipt_gap_experiment.py .]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":107,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-marker-decay","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-marker-decay.tex","caption":"With a prune threshold of , raising decay retention from to delays pruning from tick 29 to tick 59. [internal; analytic]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":37},{"id":"fig-swk-op9-reclass","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-op9-reclass.tex","caption":"One threat-table row moves through the OP-9 reclassification. The move adds partial kernel-credential defense but leaves shared-kernel and sandbox surfaces in scope; it is not proof of impossibility. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":155,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-race-dramatization","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-race-dramatization.tex","caption":"A primary-key uniqueness constraint serializes the race: the kernel grants the first insert and returns the active holder atomically to the loser. [internal, alg:acquire]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":97,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-recovery-pipeline","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-recovery-pipeline.tex","caption":"Checkpointing, page checks, and audit-link checks run before the daemon serves requests. A failed critical check blocks service. The dashed group marks separate mechanisms, not a completed shared recovery invariant.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":95,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-reference-monitor","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-reference-monitor.tex","caption":"Pre-commit mediation prevents the forbidden state. A subscriber observes it afterward and can only halt or compensate. Uniqueness constraints and boot gates mediate; the current policy monitor subscribes. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":113,"page":40},{"id":"fig-swk-rehydration-pipeline","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-rehydration-pipeline.tex","caption":"Proposed replay restores recorded inputs and durable task state, not hidden model inference state. Completeness remains unestablished; OP-4 is not closed. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":135,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-single-writer","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-single-writer.tex","caption":"Both requests arrive before the first commit. The writer orders their records and replies after each commit. This sequence assumes one writer; it does not establish power-loss durability.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":88,"page":25},{"id":"fig-swk-stack-map","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-stack-map.tex","caption":"Read upward from L0. Higher layers depend on the records beneath them, but introduce their own assumptions. The blue tick identifies this chapter. The dashed box beneath L0, the machine, is a dependency, not a fifth layer.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":82,"page":19},{"id":"fig-swk-taint-automaton","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-taint-automaton.tex","caption":"Reading a secret records taint; it is never refused. Afterward the policy blocks mediated network egress, while leaving uncontrollable events enabled. The guarantee requires the read to be observed and all relevant egress to be mediated.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":122,"page":1201},{"id":"fig-swk-ticket-lock-delta","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-ticket-lock-delta.tex","caption":"The proposed ticket queue covers cooperative release, but expiry still bypasses it. Bounded waiting remains unproved until both paths consult the queue (). [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":105,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-workunit-machine","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-workunit-machine.tex","caption":"Five guards protect the work-unit lifecycle. In the two-principal model, all 536 reachable states satisfy six invariants, which five predicates check (W5 follows from W1); removing any guard exposes the counterexample listed below. [internal, c0_workunit.py ]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":140,"page":59},{"id":"swk-unknown-effect","src":"book/figures/swk-unknown-effect.tex","caption":"A timed-out external operation leaves its effect unknown. The caller queries an operation-specific authoritative status before deciding whether to record a receipt, retry under a proved idempotent boundary, or preserve an unresolved outcome. An absence result permits retry only when the authority excludes a late commit for ; the drawing does not make unbrokered delivery exactly once [internal].","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":135,"page":601},{"id":"fig-anchor-alg-confusion","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-alg-confusion.tex","caption":"Aligned security traces hold the wire bytes constant and vary only the source of algorithm authority. Header selection reaches acceptance without a signature check; issuer pinning forces Ed25519 and rejects the same tampered token. [internal; the mechanized check is algconfusion.pv, not v1_refined.pv, which has no naive verifier]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":185,"page":92},{"id":"fig-anchor-capability-attenuation","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-capability-attenuation.tex","caption":"Every hop checks a rights subset and an expiry bound. A child may inherit its parent’s expiry when a longer lifetime is requested; it may never gain a new right.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":183,"page":90},{"id":"fig-anchor-card-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-card-lifecycle.tex","caption":"A UML state machine gives one card ID exactly two guarded terminal exits. Fresh issuance is shown separately, with no outgoing path from the revoked or expired card. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":196,"page":1011},{"id":"fig-anchor-cuckoo-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-cuckoo-inline.tex","caption":"Bitwise OR corrupts stored fingerprints; set union preserves the identifiers needed to rebuild them. Two-bucket example with one three-bit slot per bucket.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":191,"page":95},{"id":"fig-anchor-delegation-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-delegation-inline.tex","caption":"Each signature binds adjacent identities, a nonce, and the task hash. Moving a legitimate signature to another hop fails because its signed identities and nonce no longer match. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":189,"page":93},{"id":"fig-anchor-four-phases","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-four-phases.tex","caption":"Each phase adds a check without removing earlier checks. The marked step introduces the named defense under its stated assumptions. Revocation only rejects at a verifier that has received the update; no gossip deadline or universal security closure follows. [internal, Table ]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":181,"page":94},{"id":"fig-anchor-handshake-ladder","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-handshake-ladder.tex","caption":"The issue--delegate--verify ceremony as a sequence diagram. Every message after m1 falls inside the shaded region, where the Daemon is not addressed. Each card names its subject and the subject's public key. Agent A signs card_1 with its own key, and the Harbor checks each card under its signer's key: card_0 under pk_daemon , and card_1 under pk_A , the key that card_0 names. It never contacts the issuer. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":188,"page":100},{"id":"fig-anchor-revocation-gossip","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-revocation-gossip.tex","caption":"The issuing daemon stops a revoked card locally. A remote verifier can still accept while its revocation update is undelivered; gossip convergence is not a global kill switch.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":193,"page":97},{"id":"fig-anchor-v6v7-escalation","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-v6v7-escalation.tex","caption":"The capability sets are the same in both panels; only the checks change. If every link is authenticated, checking each child against its immediate parent stops re-escalation. ProVerif checks this two-link chain; subset transitivity covers longer chains.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":1021},{"id":"fig-anchor-verification-stack","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-verification-stack.tex","caption":"Obligations descend from model to source to binary; tool evidence returns upward. The two correspondence gaps still require human justification. [internal, Table ]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":198,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-composition-crossover","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-composition-crossover.tex","caption":"Analytical comparison for per-release and a fixed maximum horizon; queries may adapt. At , basic is 3.20 versus advanced 3.31. Advanced first has lower at , but allows ; basic keeps . Lower epsilon therefore trades guarantees, not uniformly stronger privacy.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":144},{"id":"fig-sealed-controllability-quadrant","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-controllability-quadrant.tex","caption":"Exact realization needs control and the relevant observations. An egress gate may miss a secret read. Observing that read permits the compound rule; denying every egress instead preserves safety while rejecting legal behavior. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":264,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-dual-attestation","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-dual-attestation.tex","caption":"One evidence bundle, two independent appraisals. Derek and Erin each release a key only after their own appraisal succeeds. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":247,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-laundering-fork","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-laundering-fork.tex","caption":"The gate is unchanged; the worker changes its argument and reveals a distinction the original parity release hid. This arithmetic example is outside C1's committed-input model. Work through the distinction in Exercise .","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":262,"page":1141},{"id":"fig-sealed-leakage-ledger","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-leakage-ledger.tex","caption":"For 200 jobs, status and three return slots allow about 13,117 bits of capacity. The ledger counts payload and timing channels separately. [hand-derived; Exercise ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":280,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-mutant-grid","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-mutant-grid.tex","caption":"Both atomicity mutants break balance immediately. Only the torn write breaches the budget cap, after three steps in this two-client model. The intact model's 15 reachable states satisfy both invariants. [internal, a3_epsilon_ledger.py ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":270,"page":143},{"id":"fig-sealed-operating-curve","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-operating-curve.tex","caption":"Three carried canaries give 99.2% conditional detection at when their misses are independent; perfectly correlated misses, as for a deliberate exfiltrator, hold detection at 80% for every (dashed). The stopping-time comparison uses , , , ; reported capped simulation means have no supplied uncertainty and do not certify error control.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":277,"page":147},{"id":"fig-sealed-pillar-pipeline","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-pillar-pipeline.tex","caption":"Each owner authorizes removal of their own restriction. Dashed links bind controls to the signed work order; solid arrows carry outputs. Proposed control flow; public receipt omitted.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":255,"page":134},{"id":"fig-sealed-receipt-provenance","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-receipt-provenance.tex","caption":"Hashes and the signature bind the recorded work order, evidence, inputs, model, policy state, and released ciphertext. The receipt proves what was reported, not that the output is true.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":251,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-release-lattice","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-release-lattice.tex","caption":"Four artifact labels and four owner-controlled release steps. An arrow in the diamond adds a restriction; the table names the authority needed to remove one. A release gate may exercise delegated authority within its contract. Releasing an artifact does not make the worker clean: after a secret read, whole-worker taint persists until job destruction.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":249,"page":1151},{"id":"fig-sealed-residuals-converge","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-residuals-converge.tex","caption":"Alternative outputs share one -bit envelope. A claimed privacy parameter is not a bit count. Timing and other unmodeled side channels lie outside this accounting bound.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":279,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-three-principals","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-three-principals.tex","caption":"The sealed room contains the computation, not its owners or host. Derek supplies data and Erin supplies a model over encrypted input channels; attestation binds their release to the intended workload. Authorized outputs leave through separate release gates. The claim assumes the chapter's confidential-computing boundary and does not eliminate excluded hardware side channels.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":239,"page":1161},{"id":"fig-sealed-two-adversaries","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-two-adversaries.tex","caption":"The same ledger conserves declared spend, not semantic privacy. DP needs valid mechanisms and complete mediation; bounds only the specified output channel before timing. [internal, ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":269,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-two-worlds","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-two-worlds.tex","caption":"Parity hides the difference between secrets 0 and 2; a raw-secret release exposes it. Reported model check: four secrets, depth 7, not unbounded executions. [internal, c1_noninterference.py ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":260,"page":137},{"id":"fig-sealed-work-order-schema","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-work-order-schema.tex","caption":"The work order binds measurements, permitted execution, recipients, limits, and remedies. A digest identifies approved content; an attestation binds the reported runtime measurement. Neither implements the checks or proves correctness. Changed contract bytes require fresh matching signatures under the hash and signature assumptions. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":246,"page":600},{"id":"fig-legible-halving-tree","src":"book/figures/fig-legible-halving-tree.tex","caption":"A constructed halving trace with positive item . Every box is one group query; only positive nonsingletons split. Negative groups certify all their members at once. The saving counts noiseless, unit-cost queries, not elapsed time or bytes scanned.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":347,"page":1131},{"id":"legible-swarm-completion-verifier","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-completion-verifier.tex","caption":"Vision: a proposed authority-side rule, not implemented enforcement or a guarantee of universal correctness. Passing it still leaves any omitted requirement unchecked.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":321,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-consent-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-consent-lifecycle.tex","caption":"Vision. Permission is not execution, and an action decision does not renew the grant.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":302,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-escalation-band","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-escalation-band.tex","caption":"With the chapter's stated model, no false-escalation debit meets both constraints for an attention budget below . At a budget of , the feasible interval is . An empty band requires more capacity or better evidence. [verified, b7_escalation_band.py ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":178},{"id":"legible-swarm-hayek-scott","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-hayek-scott.tex","caption":"Scott and Hayek offer complementary cautions: administrative legibility can erase local knowledge. The arrows motivate a design proposal; they do not prove a universal bottleneck or an effective intervention. [interpretive synthesis]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":380,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-heavy-tails","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-heavy-tails.tex","caption":"The two-moment formula overstates the pool's delay, most where the pool has servers to spare. Simulated mean wait in queue over the Allen--Cunneen value, at a squared coefficient of variation of 6. Each point is 32 runs of 4 million jobs, and its 95% interval is no taller than its marker. [internal, b8_heavy_tails.py ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":1251},{"id":"legible-swarm-heavy-tails-crossing","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-heavy-tails-crossing.tex","caption":"The speed a specialist needs to match the pool, in multiples of one generalist's speed, at . The exponential column is exact. The others are at a squared coefficient of variation of 6, and the simulated ones are known to within (95% interval). [internal, b8_heavy_tails.py ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":1261},{"id":"legible-swarm-inception-canary","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-inception-canary.tex","caption":"Two proposed responses to a sandboxed defect replay. The replay cannot modify production; score-driven changes to future grants still require policy limits and evaluation. Other responses need separate scoring rules. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":335,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-judge-dependence","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-judge-dependence.tex","caption":"Three reviewers have separate principal identities but read the same source and make identical errors on two of four constructed items. Distinct principals remove one conflict of interest; they do not by themselves prove independent errors. Error dependence needs labeled evaluation, while strategic collusion remains a separate question [constructed example].","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":313,"page":621},{"id":"legible-swarm-obligation-coverage","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-obligation-coverage.tex","caption":"A six-unit context pack selects A (four units) and C (two units), covering R1, R2, and R4. R3 remains blocked because its sole source B is outside the reader's disclosure scope. The receipt reports declared coverage and the missing requirement; it proves neither semantic completeness nor effect authority [constructed example].","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":375,"page":631},{"id":"legible-swarm-plan-revision","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-plan-revision.tex","caption":"Receipt reuse depends on what changed. Source edits invalidate compile and acceptance evidence; policy edits require fresh acceptance; revocation blocks publication. Unknown external effects still require reconciliation. Constructed contract, not an implemented invalidation algorithm.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":312,"page":611},{"id":"legible-swarm-rate-regime","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-rate-regime.tex","caption":"At , the positive-rate wedge lies between and ; the zero-rate boundary enters at and continues above-left outside the panel.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-roles","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-roles.tex","caption":"The operator grants once; the daemon gates or escalates each subsequent act. Operator override bypasses agents. A live fleet repeats the act-and-check pair, not the grant. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":379,"page":211},{"id":"legible-swarm-sa-levels","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-sa-levels.tex","caption":"A read surface can expose evidence without establishing the operator's situation awareness.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":333,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-sdt","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-sdt.tex","caption":"Lowering the threshold trades missed dangers for false alarms without changing sensitivity. These Gaussian shapes use an arbitrary vertical scale; is their mean separation divided by their common standard deviation. The drawn threshold is illustrative, not a fitted optimum. [internal, Definition ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":329,"page":180},{"id":"legible-swarm-specialization","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-specialization.tex","caption":"At three agents, pooling wins below and sole ownership above it. The dashed, superseded threshold diverges incorrectly; the worked point narrowly favours sole ownership. [internal; closed form]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":175},{"id":"legible-swarm-split-ranker","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-split-ranker.tex","caption":"Synthetic preferences: (a) fits one common ranking; (b) reverses briefing and attention, so no ranking is optimal for both at every selection budget. Panels compare preferences, not time or measured scores.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":200},{"id":"legible-swarm-state-of-nature","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-state-of-nature.tex","caption":"Three worked traces start from one settings.json revision. A keywise merge is benign; a raw splice fails immediately; a valid exclusion stays green until release replay exposes the hidden fixture. [internal, pedagogical counterexample]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":297,"page":160},{"id":"legible-swarm-zoom-advantage","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-zoom-advantage.tex","caption":"Two sufficient certificates, not measured performance curves. Plain halving's ratio is piecewise hyperbolic, with jumps at inverse powers of two, and guarantees fewer queries than flat inspection below . Hwang's splitting, for a tester who knows , guarantees it below . Failure of a certificate does not establish a loss: evenly spread positives among items require halving queries.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":1211},{"id":"legible-swarm-zoom-vs-potemkin","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-zoom-vs-potemkin.tex","caption":"Two claim trees of identical shape. Top: the legible digest's three named claims each resolve to one artifact: a diff, a test run, a review comment. Bottom: a same-shaped summary whose three claims resolve to nothing an operator can open. A safe summary is an index into evidence; a calm one that terminates early is a Potemkin digest, whichever claim count it advertises [internal].","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":307,"page":167},{"id":"fig-audit-person","src":"book/figures/fig-audit-person.tex","caption":"Processes come and go; the account they write to is what the book calls a person. Reputation is what that account's confirmed record is worth to the next buyer. [constructed example]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":1231},{"id":"fig-stp-audit-amortization","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-audit-amortization.tex","caption":"Continuous integrals are curves; discrete bills at are dots: , , . Model B plateaus at continuously versus discretely; its first zero-rate grade is . Model A keeps growing. Parameters and sums are in the text.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":464,"page":600},{"id":"fig-stp-dependency-spine","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-dependency-spine.tex","caption":"Each higher tier requires the foundation below it; none follows from that foundation alone. T0--T4 name capability tiers, distinct from architecture layers L0--L3. The status labels separate implemented logs and partial summary restart from specified reputation and proposed trade. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":404,"page":600},{"id":"fig-stp-deterrence-regime","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-deterrence-regime.tex","caption":"Deterrence requires . For , the threshold is ; lower audit probability makes capture profitable. [internal; closed form]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":273},{"id":"fig-stp-engine-swap-regime","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-engine-swap-regime.tex","caption":"Common prices leave the cost-saving incentive intact. Attested prices deter substitution only when their gap covers . Analytic example: , , , ; no audited bond or future reputation payoff (Theorem ).","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":441,"page":1171},{"id":"fig-stp-handoff-coverage","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-handoff-coverage.tex","caption":"An intact selection can omit a required instruction. Synthetic old fixture, handoff-coverage experiment of 20 September 2026, run 03; source functions tested with scanners stubbed. No provider behaviour or source recovery was tested.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":422,"page":600},{"id":"fig-stp-judge-market","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-judge-market.tex","caption":"Before selection, exclusions and a public draw support neutrality. After selection, a bond and later re-audit support accountability. Both stages leave checkable evidence. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":456,"page":1181},{"id":"fig-stp-multidim-reputation","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-multidim-reputation.tex","caption":"A favours accuracy and aesthetics; B favours efficiency. Different buyer priorities legitimately reverse the ranking. A universal average would erase that choice. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":454,"page":265},{"id":"fig-stp-nomint-lineage","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-nomint-lineage.tex","caption":"Transfer spends each source balance; an undebited copy retains it. The first row counts inherited priors, the others spendable balances.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":415,"page":241},{"id":"fig-stp-parfit-chain","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-parfit-chain.tex","caption":"An engineering analogy inspired by Parfit's overlapping chains. Assume valid succession records connect incarnations 1 to 2 and 2 to 3; the shared outcome witnesses make those handoffs inspectable. The chain establishes directed ledger ancestry, not psychological identity or a symmetric equivalence. Reusing an outcome identifier alone does not validate a handoff. A repeated label without a valid succession record inherits no ledger. [illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":411,"page":239},{"id":"fig-stp-probation-cliff","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-probation-cliff.tex","caption":"At , delaying equal deterrence raises the newcomer's burden by . Front-loading is undominated; 4,000 searched instances found no improvement. [internal, b6_probation.py , seed 20260816]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":251},{"id":"fig-stp-rate-the-raters","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-rate-the-raters.tex","caption":"Exact recursions at , a gain no audit rate deters at level 0. With , conditional detection gives , first below the bribe price at . The dashed trace additionally assumes a self-funded, non-replenishing budget: subtract while , then multiply by , first below at . A sound terminal judge is a separate requirement. These are model values, not measured audit performance.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":270},{"id":"fig-stp-resurrection-soundness","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-resurrection-soundness.tex","caption":"Each safeguard blocks a different modeled escape. Trace lengths count actions in the bounded search, not time or deployment incidents. Clause (iii) includes the required escrow adjustment before cutover. [verified, b5_engine_substitution.py ]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":442,"page":1191},{"id":"fig-stp-role-vs-person","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-role-vs-person.tex","caption":"A role stays while its occupants change. A person's witnessed record stays while bodies and roles change. Reputation belongs to that continuing identity, not the slot. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":407,"page":236},{"id":"fig-stp-sybil-whitewash","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-sybil-whitewash.tex","caption":"Principal-linked policies retain a sanction and count one vote. Free unlinkable resets remove that sanction; per-label voting counts votes. Illustrative rules within one enrollment domain: authentication alone enforces neither policy. [internal, illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":435,"page":253},{"id":"fig-stp-tombstone","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-tombstone.tex","caption":"A tombstone removes a fraudulent contribution from future scoring without erasing history. Importing harbors remain exposed until it arrives; measures that convergence interval. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":469,"page":276},{"id":"fig-audit-loop","src":"book/figures/fig-audit-loop.tex","caption":"Every pair agrees, yet the whole does not: the loop returns 1.2, not 1, so no single price list fits all three quotes. [constructed example]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":1241},{"id":"fig-he-assurance","src":"book/figures/fig-he-assurance.tex","caption":"In this analytic model, more independent reviewers reduce miss probability; perfectly shared outcomes do not. The lower panel is reserved budget, not realized payout.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":541,"page":330},{"id":"fig-he-cold-start","src":"book/figures/fig-he-cold-start.tex","caption":"Pricing follows realized liquidity, not calendar time. Suppliers are paid to join, then work is free, and buyers are charged only above ; a market that never crosses the threshold never charges. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":535,"page":318},{"id":"fig-he-conflict-kinds","src":"book/figures/fig-he-conflict-kinds.tex","caption":"A policy can contain several conflicts: these counts are not disjoint shares. Synthetic sweep of policies, seed ; b4_deontic_fragment.py .","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":516,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-conflict-witness","src":"book/figures/fig-he-conflict-witness.tex","caption":"Inference activates ; the unconditional prohibition covers . The Horn-ablated checker misses this witness and of the conflicting cases in the -policy seeded sweep. [verified, b4_deontic_fragment.py ]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":1091},{"id":"fig-he-conservation-functor","src":"book/figures/fig-he-conservation-functor.tex","caption":"Within , the illustrated wallet, escrow, and commons deltas sum to zero. A conversion records its rate, time, recipient amount, fee, and the execution shortfall relative to its quote; later rate movement remains an open exposure. [internal; illustrative values]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":521,"page":309},{"id":"fig-he-deontic-frontier","src":"book/figures/fig-he-deontic-frontier.tex","caption":"Monotone inference determines the fired rules. Disjunctive obligations require a globally compatible selection; checking a supplied selection remains polynomial. The 3-SAT reduction proves the worst-case boundary; seeded instances check its encoding. The reference script uses pair enumeration, not the indexed bound above. [verified, b4_deontic_fragment.py ]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":515,"page":1101},{"id":"fig-he-deterrence-convention","src":"book/figures/fig-he-deterrence-convention.tex","caption":"Same , , ; different forfeiture. Keep-gain takes , requiring audit rate . Claw-back takes , requiring . [analytic example]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-float-plan","src":"book/figures/fig-he-float-plan.tex","caption":"Proposed reservation order: requester bounty and provider bond are reserved together. The worker waits for the reservation receipt. The signed ceremony and enforced gate are not yet complete. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":299},{"id":"fig-he-ms-wedge","src":"book/figures/fig-he-ms-wedge.tex","caption":"Independent uniform values and costs on ,cr are an illustrative prior, not market data. The marked rental offers ,cr of surplus, below this equilibrium's ,cr trade threshold.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-rater-ladder","src":"book/figures/fig-he-rater-ladder.tex","caption":"Each appeal lowers a natural-number rank and stops at rank zero. That endpoint may be a protected oracle or a named final authority; termination does not turn preferences into objective truth. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":773,"page":1111},{"id":"fig-he-skill-lineage","src":"book/figures/fig-he-skill-lineage.tex","caption":"A versioned skill document binds v2 to its v1 parent while retaining a separate v2 evaluation root. The displayed counts illustrate a predeclared discounted prior, not evidence that v2 behaves like v1. [internal; illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":767,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-succession-price","src":"book/figures/fig-he-succession-price.tex","caption":"Chosen rates: task/h, /h and /h. The limiting lower bound exceeds the pool's h-equivalent cost, so increased skill alone cannot win here. Analytic model, not measurements.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":314},{"id":"fig-he-three-sided","src":"book/figures/fig-he-three-sided.tex","caption":"One refactor, three alternative purchases. Rental and licensing are designed, not shipped; all three use the same escrow. [illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":496,"page":294},{"id":"fig-he-two-bucket-settlement","src":"book/figures/fig-he-two-bucket-settlement.tex","caption":"Separate payment and performance-collateral balances settle by different rules. Success releases Carol's flat CR licence fee. Partial pays of the bounty and returns of the bond; the other CR goes to the commons. Amounts are disbursements, not net earnings. [constructed example]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":510,"page":1121},{"id":"tab-keystone-split","src":"book/figures/tab-keystone-split.tex","caption":"What crosses the trust boundary. Bob can check every row from outside Alice's harbor except the last: a signed, intact history still does not prove who controls the foreign key. The market needs that row and does not have it yet. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[5,6],"shared":true,"bookPage":null,"page":284},{"id":"fig-bc-delta-threshold","src":"book/figures/fig-bc-delta-threshold.tex","caption":"Three-round punishment caps the loss; grim punishment does not. The curves assume shared, correct observations and no bond. The square is the archived four-round TLC counterexample, not a measured payoff series.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":601,"page":388},{"id":"fig-bonded-cartel-folk-theorem-tikz","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-cartel-folk-theorem-tikz.tex","caption":"S means the cartel sustains; C means it collapses. Every simulated boundary lies within one tested grid step of the closed-form threshold (). Each configuration uses 5 , 000 trials, 200 rounds, and three colluders. [verified, proofs/bonded/pareto/simulation-cartel.mjs ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":616,"page":378},{"id":"fig-bonded-conservation-ledger","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-conservation-ledger.tex","caption":"Only top-up increases supply. A partial breach moves from to : the full escrow closes, while total supply stays 10. [internal, Conservation.tla ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":627,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-inclusion-check","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-inclusion-check.tex","caption":"Two sibling hashes connect receipt to a four-record tree. Accept only when a trusted-key signature verifies and the roots match. The proof establishes inclusion, not truth.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":581,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-isolation-ladder","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-isolation-ladder.tex","caption":"Three editing arrangements. Advisory claims report overlap; separate worktrees separate ordinary edits. is the chapter's declared default. The arrows name mechanisms, not a security order: shared credentials may still permit access across worktrees, and integration conflicts remain. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":576,"page":1031},{"id":"fig-bonded-key-custody","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-key-custody.tex","caption":"Each attack requires different access. These conditions exclude same-user code execution on the daemon host. [design invariant]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":636,"page":390},{"id":"fig-bonded-merkle-forest","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-merkle-forest.tex","caption":"Two inclusion paths connect a note to a signed checkpoint of the harbor log. Here, the hashes and signature occupy 736 bytes. [hand-derived]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":580,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-regiment-boundary","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-regiment-boundary.tex","caption":"Complete mediation and atomic admission can prevent violations, including operations authorized by remote permits. Evidence available only after an irreversible effect supports detection and recovery. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":577,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-session-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-session-lifecycle.tex","caption":"Session and queue states are different carriers in the lifecycle model of Section . Crash changes no session status; Salvage changes only the queue. Reap updates both records atomically. Dismiss requires a pending queue entry, deletes it and the session, and deregisters the agent. Settlement recipients and an eventual-recovery fairness condition are not supplied by this model. [design model; not model-checked]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":622,"page":1041},{"id":"fig-bonded-sybil-deposit-floor-tikz","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-sybil-deposit-floor-tikz.tex","caption":"Reimbursing the commons does not eliminate attacker profit. Under the specified bids, loss distribution, zero funding costs, and coverage-capped slashing, one or three Sybil identities remain profitable across the tested deposits. Full forfeiture is not simulated. [verified, proofs/bonded/pareto/simulation-sybil.mjs ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":614,"page":376},{"id":"fig-bonded-trust-collision","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-trust-collision.tex","caption":"Two uncoordinated agents edit and push the same file, ninety seconds apart. The second push conflicts; an invented resolution corrupts it. This is the chapter's opening scenario. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":565,"page":600},{"id":"fig-cartel-game-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-cartel-game-inline.tex","caption":"For collusive margin , , negligible undercutting ( ), and , the boundary is . Deviation pays above; collusion below. Marks show and . Model values, not measurements. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[6,7],"shared":true,"bookPage":null,"page":377},{"id":"fig-governance-flow","src":"book/figures/fig-governance-flow.tex","caption":"Dispute resolution is an ordered four-stage escalation ladder. Each stage badge is keyed to the escalation trigger in the legend, and every stage outcome (released, expired, preempted, or ruled) is written to the same evidence record, whichever stage resolved the dispute. Escalation therefore changes only the decision cost and decision-maker, never the record kept for appeal. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":588,"page":356},{"id":"fig-magic-link-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-magic-link-inline.tex","caption":"Overlapping requests still produce one consumption. A wins this illustrated schedule; either caller can win. SQL is simplified: authentication and expiry checks are omitted.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":636,"page":391},{"id":"fig-pareto-dominance-tikz","src":"book/figures/fig-pareto-dominance-tikz.tex","caption":"Simulation frequencies for the tolerance-based comparison defined in the text. A fixes ; B fixes noise and collusion at zero. Each point uses 2 , 000 trials of 50 transactions. [simulation, simulation.mjs]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":612,"page":375},{"id":"fig-sen-pareto-locking","src":"book/figures/fig-sen-pareto-locking.tex","caption":"Precautionary locks versus advisory claims. In panel (a), agent 's decisive lock on an unneeded file aborts agent 's task . In panel (b), advisory notification lets release , achieving the Pareto-superior outcome where both tasks succeed.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":585,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sybil-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-sybil-inline.tex","caption":"Under the analyzed coverage-capped contract, extra identities require extra posted capital. Slashing stops at coverage ; deposits above that cap cannot increase the loss. Figure tests the resulting incentives. [internal, closed form]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":613,"page":375},{"id":"fig-worked-example","src":"book/figures/fig-worked-example.tex","caption":"Three layers share one wall-clock axis. Process authority ends at minute 12 and a successor receives a new capability at minute 13. The evidence chain bridges the crash through a salvage-parent edge, while the pre-funded $6 escrow remains live until settlement at minute 24. The crash therefore disposes of identity without disposing of attribution or cleanup exposure. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":568,"page":400},{"id":"fig-fh-cochain-hand","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-cochain-hand.tex","caption":"The residual fits edge differences: a size- offset gives on the ring and on each acyclic visible graph. A zero residual does not certify the underlying reports. Direct equality requires the same authenticated sender, coordinate and claim context; different senders or epochs may legitimately differ. [verified, scalar closed form]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":675,"page":1051},{"id":"fig-fh-conservation-ledger","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-conservation-ledger.tex","caption":"Whole-bond status, not recipient balances. Clearance may divide funds among payment, remainder, and fee. This cross-harbor partition is a conditional design invariant. The recorded TLC result concerns the separate single-machine Conservation model; cross-harbor custody and recipient conservation need their own verification. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":694,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-cycle-vs-cut","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-cycle-vs-cut.tex","caption":"One-edge perturbation of size 3: the cycle residual is ; the path residual is zero. This is an edge-cochain diagnostic. Authenticated endpoint claims can be compared directly on either topology. Analytic construction.","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":677,"page":1061},{"id":"fig-fh-revocation-gossip","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-revocation-gossip.tex","caption":"One illustrative delivery trace, not an expectation or bound: refuses immediately, after , and after . A partition can extend staleness without bound. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":668,"page":419},{"id":"fig-fh-revocation-regime","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-revocation-regime.tex","caption":"Expiry closes the window when operational guarantees are weaker. Without a partition bound, only expiry remains. The eight-round TTL is illustrative, not a measured deployment setting.","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":670,"page":420},{"id":"fig-fh-settle-protocol","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-settle-protocol.tex","caption":"Posting a bond and announcing damage do not settle it. The escrow, as custodian, checks the proofs and the adjudicator's ruling against the signed terms, then makes one terminal move: clear or refuse. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":694,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-settlement","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-settlement.tex","caption":"With a non-bypassable gate, recipient whitelist, and fee cap, custody closes only by payment or refund. Adding an operator-controlled escape exposes the entire balance, not merely the fee. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":690,"page":1071},{"id":"fig-fh-sovereignty-fence","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-sovereignty-fence.tex","caption":"Alice can issue a valid card; she cannot make Bob accept it. This refusal precedes the transfer ceremony. [illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":656,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-sponsor-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-sponsor-lifecycle.tex","caption":"Shown paths from probation: graduation after funded replacement, or expulsion for misconduct. Misconduct forfeits the sponsor's bond, giving a reason to vet the newcomer. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":698,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-threat-bands","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-threat-bands.tex","caption":"Cross-realm identity and replay remain conditional on signature checks and fresh roots; their protocol proof is pending. The available capability models concern a single harbor. Revocation and settlement depend on connectivity and custody assumptions. Joining, cartel monitoring and concentration of control remain open. Positions indicate qualitative assurance. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":661,"page":415},{"id":"fig-fh-worked-example","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-worked-example.tex","caption":"One constructed incident across five authorities. (1) Alice's harbor offers a transfer. (2) Carol's staging harbor authorizes its own resource mapping and executes. (3--4) Bob's harbor detects the mismatch and submits evidence, with inclusion proofs against the staging root and its own. (5) The adjudicator named in the bond's terms rules; the escrow, as custodian, pays the cleanup cost to Bob, the listed beneficiary, and refunds the remainder. (6) Alice's harbor publishes revocation; later gossip has no guaranteed delivery deadline. Inclusion proves record membership, not causation. [internal; constructed example]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":699,"page":1081},{"id":"fig-fh-xfer-ceremony","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-xfer-ceremony.tex","caption":"Only the offer and acknowledgement cross the boundary, and neither carries the bearer card : the offer is 's signed attestation of it, naming the holder, the recipient and a transfer identifier. The displayed subset relation assumes the same resource identifiers. A different resource needs a new grant under 's policy. Local verification uses 's public key and the holder's proof of possession, and must enforce the parent-revocation dependency. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":663,"page":416},{"id":"tab-fh-partition","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-partition.tex","caption":"Partition behavior is protocol-specific. Transfer needs current evidence; revocation spreads within reachable components. Settlement follows agreed hold, timeout and refund rules; recovery has no automatic deadline. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":707,"page":600},{"id":"tab-fh-revocation-rules","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-revocation-rules.tex","caption":"Three candidate revocation-conflict rules, evaluated against the same disagreement (harbor has revoked card ; harbor has not yet seen it). The adopted rule is the only one with a bounded attacker window under stated assumptions. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":672,"page":600},{"id":"tab-fh-sheaf-harness","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-sheaf-harness.tex","caption":"Equal-information detection on synthetic trials. The direct checker groups sender claims; the residual receives edge differences derived from the same visible records. [verified, sheaf_harness_v2.py ]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"tab-fh-topology","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-topology.tex","caption":"Four message channels connect sovereign harbors without a shared signing root. Witnessing authorizes nothing; settlement's custody bound depends on its gate being non-bypassable. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"tab-fh-witness-log","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-witness-log.tex","caption":"Five witness-log properties, each closing a distinct federation failure. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":658,"page":600}];
